{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Pass before the people.</b> And see whether they stone you — why did you bring disgrace upon my sons? (Shemot Rabbah)." "<b>And take with you some of the elders of Israel.</b> For testimony — that they would see that through your hand water comes forth from the rock, and they would not say: there were springs there from before." "<b>And your staff with which you struck the river.</b> What does Scripture tell — ״אֲשֶׁר הִכִּיתָ בּוֹ אֶת הַיְאֹר״? Rather, Israel would say of the staff that it is designated only for punishment — with it Pharaoh and Egypt were struck by many plagues in Egypt and at the Sea. Therefore it says ״אֲשֶׁר הִכִּיתָ בּוֹ אֶת הַיְאֹר״ — let them see now that for good too it is designated (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:50.581538637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}